# The cells that fail outright, at either level, with no row to take the
# finding.
cancel/applied/primary-killed-unannounced/t1-left ADR-0055 §11  # unannounced: the callee's 180 is lost with the node, so the caller never rings and never CANCELs; the callee's 200 then takes the call over and answers it
cancel/off/primary-killed-unannounced/t1-applied ADR-0055 §11  # unannounced: the callee's 180 is lost with the node, so the caller never rings and never CANCELs; the callee's 200 then takes the call over and answers it
cancel/off/primary-killed-unannounced/t1-left ADR-0055 §11  # unannounced: the callee's 180 is lost with the node, so the caller never rings and never CANCELs; the callee's 200 then takes the call over and answers it
refer/applied/primary-killed-unannounced/t5-logged ADR-0055 §11  # unannounced: the backup applied the write of bob's REFER the dead primary logged; bob's retransmission reaches it after the verdict and is read as a second REFER (491 Request Pending), so the transfer never completes
refer/applied/primary-rebooted/t5-applied ADR-0055 §11  # the transfer's outside answer lost with the node; alice waits for the merge, and no row's predicate takes it
refer/applied/primary-rebooted/t5-left ADR-0055 §11  # the transfer's outside answer lost with the node; alice waits for the merge, and no row's predicate takes it
refer/off/primary-killed-unannounced/t5-left ADR-0055 §11  # unannounced: no message reaches the backup before the force-delete: nothing the parties repeat reaches it, so what the dead primary began waits and a party's own timer fires first
refer/off/primary-killed-unannounced/t5-logged ADR-0055 §11  # unannounced: the backup applied the write of bob's REFER the dead primary logged; bob's retransmission reaches it after the verdict and is read as a second REFER (491 Request Pending), so the transfer never completes
